course: dictionary
lesson: 12360
title: Criteria: the rules for judging
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A criterion is a rule or standard you use to judge or decide something. Standard means the level something must reach. «The judges used three criteria to choose the winner: neatness, accuracy and effort.» The clue words are judges, choose and winner, so criteria must be the things the judges checked.
explain: Your teacher may give you success criteria before a task. These are the steps that show you did the task well. «Our success criteria are a clear title, two facts and full stops at the end of every sentence.» If you check each step, you know your work is good.
explain: Remember that one is a criterion and more than one is criteria. Do not write criterias. «One criterion for the science fair was that every test must be fair.»
fact: A criterion is a rule or standard used to judge or decide something.
fact: Criteria is the plural of criterion: one criterion, two or more criteria.
fact: Success criteria are the steps a teacher says show you did a task well.
fact: Criteria are used in school, in science experiments, in competitions and in jobs.
fact: «The judges used three criteria to choose the winner» means the judges used rules to decide who won.
exercise: «The teacher shared the success criteria before we started writing.» What are success criteria? | The name of the classroom | The homework for the week | *The steps that show you did the task well | A kind of pencil
exercise: «The judges used three criteria to choose the winner.» What were the judges doing with the criteria? | Eating their lunch | Painting the hall | Losing the game | *Deciding who won
exercise: Which word is the plural of criterion? | criterias | *criteria | criterium
test: «Our criteria for a good poster are a clear title and neat writing.» What does a criterion help you do? | Remember the date | Draw a picture | *Judge or decide if something is good | Run faster
test: Ravi has one ___ for judging the race. Which word fits the gap? | criteria | *criterion | criterions
exam: Ms Lee says, «Read the success criteria before you start.» Why should you read them first? | *So you know which steps show a good job | So you can skip the task | So you can copy a friend | So you can finish quickly without thinking
